            <ArticleTitle>Protrusion of a peritoneal catheter through the umblicus: an unusual complication of a ventriculoperitoneal shunt.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>171-2</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Protrusion of a ventriculoperitoneal (VP) shunt through the umblicus is one of the rare complications of shunt insertion reported in the medical literature. One such case is presented here in a child in whom a VP shunt had been placed for congenital hydrocephalus.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
